course: dictionary
lesson: 14946
title: Bringing it back
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A reintroduction is when something is brought back to a place or a way it used to be. The prefix re- means again, and introduce means bring in, so reintroduction means bringing back again.
explain: «The reintroduction of beavers to the river gave the fish a better home.» The beavers were gone, and now they are back in the river where they used to live. So reintroduction means bringing an animal back to its old home.
explain: Reintroduction can also mean bringing back a rule or a product. «The reintroduction of the old lunch rule surprised everyone.» Nobody had seen that rule for years, so it came back again.
fact: Reintroduction is a noun. You can say a reintroduction or reintroductions.
fact: The prefix re- means again, so reintroduce means introduce again.
fact: Reintroduction often means bringing an animal or plant back to a place it used to live.
fact: In conservation, a reintroduction programme helps endangered species, which are animals or plants at risk of dying out.
fact: «The reintroduction of wolves» is a phrase you may see in science and news reports.
exercise: «The reintroduction of the red squirrel helped the wood.» What does reintroduction mean here? | A brand-new squirrel that has never lived anywhere before | Cutting down all the trees in the wood | *Bringing the squirrel back to the wood where it used to live | Feeding squirrels in a park
exercise: What does the prefix re- in reintroduction mean? | Very large | Under | *Again | Not at all
exercise: The council brought back the old bus rule after ten years. What is this called? | Extinction | Invention | Recipe | *Reintroduction
test: «The reintroduction programme brought the otters back to the river.» What did the programme do? | *It brought otters back to a river where they used to live | It counted the fish in the sea | It took otters away from the river | It built a new river from nothing
test: Which sentence shows a rule being brought back? | «The dog ran across the park.» | *«The reintroduction of the old lunch rule made everyone groan.» | «The rain fell all afternoon.» | «The class painted a big kite in art.»
exam: Which best explains reintroduction in «The reintroduction of wolves helped the forest»? | To hunt wolves until none are left | To paint pictures of wolves | *To bring wolves back into the forest where they used to live | To count the trees in the forest
